  "Event.Trigger.Guide.1": "Round trigger | TriggerValue: round parameters / range (array); Location is usually empty. Match the array length of existing events in the same scenario.",
  "Event.Trigger.Guide.2": "Capture trigger | Location: array of target region IDs; TriggerValue: usually the target country or a condition parameter. At least one Location is expected.",
  "Event.Trigger.Guide.3": "Attack trigger | Location: can restrict the trigger region; TriggerValue: object / country condition defined by the scenario. Region triggers need the attack-event gate enabled in the map data first.",
  "Event.Trigger.Guide.4": "Attack or air-raid trigger | Same as 3, but an air raid also satisfies it. Location can restrict the region; TriggerValue holds the matching condition parameters.",
  "Event.Trigger.Guide.5": "Chained / delayed trigger | TriggerValue[0]: ID of the preceding event; further entries are delay / parameters. The preceding ID must exist; avoid self-reference loops.",
  "Event.Trigger.Guide.6": "General defeated trigger | TriggerValue: general ID; Location is optional and restricts where it can happen. The general ID should exist in GeneralSettings.",
  "Event.Trigger.Guide.7": "Nuke / special attack trigger | Location: monitored regions; TriggerValue: extra conditions. If it depends on a region, fill in at least one Location.",
  "Event.Trigger.Guide.8": "City / capital count threshold | TriggerValue: the count threshold; Location is usually empty or limited to scenario regions. Use a non-negative integer.",
  "Event.Trigger.Guide.9": "Shared probability | TriggerValue: parameters decided by the group configuration; Chance is still this event's hit probability. Behaviour differs between versions, so follow verified records of the same scenario.",
  "Event.Trigger.Guide.10": "All cities lost | Location: must list the monitored region IDs; TriggerValue is usually empty. The regions need a matching loss-event gate.",
  "Event.Trigger.GuideCustom": "Custom Trigger ({0}) | Any integer is accepted. No usage guide is recorded for this value; follow existing events of the same kind when filling TriggerValue / Location.",

